  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Country Programme for Iraq</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Government of Iraq formally requested on January 2024 UNIDO#s assistance through a Country Programme. This request was confirmed during the visit of H.E. Mr. Fuad Hussein Deputy Prime Minister for International Relations Affairs and Minister for Foreign Affairs of the Republic of Iraq to UNIDO#s headquarters on 22 January 2024. Iraq#s economic trajectory has been tumultuous for a number of reasons starting with its reliance on oil revenue, conflict against the Islamic State, as well as the COVID-19 pandemic. However, in 2023, the government passed its largest budget to date, slated to remain in effect until 2025, aimed at addressing developmental needs. Priorities include investing in infrastructure, job creation, and reconstruction efforts to foster inclusive and sustainable growth. UNIDO and Iraq aim to address these issues through CP Iraq, focusing on economic diversification, industrial policy, MSME development, Industry 4.0, quality infrastructure, food security, decarbonization, and circular economy initiatives. The CP aligns with Iraq Vision 2030, emphasizing sustainable development and governance. It aims to create a diversified economy, generate secure jobs, and stabilize the country&apos;s development trajectory. Social cohesion and gender equality are highlighted, along with resilience, re covery, and</narrative>
  </description>
